bottled-openweb-ui
==================

This repository packages Open WebUI for Cloud in a Bottle / OpenHost.

Open WebUI
----------
This image is built FROM the official Open WebUI container image and
distributes Open WebUI, a self-hosted web interface for large language models.

  Upstream:    https://github.com/open-webui/open-webui
  License:     Open WebUI License (a BSD-3-Clause-style license with an added
               branding-protection clause), Copyright (c) 2023- Open WebUI Inc.
               [Created by Timothy Jaeryang Baek]
  Base image:  ghcr.io/open-webui/open-webui:v0.9.5 (see the FROM line in the
               Dockerfile)

The full Open WebUI License is reproduced in LICENSE, as its terms require the
copyright notice and conditions to be retained on redistribution. Note clause 4
of that license: the "Open WebUI" branding must not be removed or altered
(subject to the stated exceptions). This package does not modify Open WebUI or
its branding; the startup wrapper only adapts data paths, disables Open WebUI's
own login (the Cloud in a Bottle router gates to the owner), pins the public
URL, and wires up the model provider.

Third-party components
----------------------
The image additionally installs mitmproxy (mitmdump), used locally to front the
Bifrost LLM gateway as an OpenAI-compatible endpoint.

  mitmproxy:   https://github.com/mitmproxy/mitmproxy  (MIT License)

